I originally noticed and fixed this in my PR for the Gradient editor. Only now found that it's a broader issue.

Code I used to fix this in the Gradient Editor, which might help:

```cpp
Size2 minsize = popup->get_contents_minimum_size();
bool show_above = false;
if (get_global_position().y + get_size().y + minsize.y > get_viewport_rect().size.y) {
	// Not enough space below. Draw above in one of two conditions:
	// 1. There is enough space above.
	// 2. The gradient editor's center is below the middle of the screen.
	if (get_global_position().y >= minsize.y || get_global_position().y * 2 + get_size().y > get_viewport_rect().size.y) {
		show_above = true;
	}
}

if (show_above) {
	popup->set_position(get_screen_position() - Vector2(0, minsize.y));
} else {
	popup->set_position(get_screen_position() + Vector2(0, get_size().y));
}
	popup->popup();
```

Also it looks like the popup direction is determined in `color_picker.cpp`, the `void ColorPickerButton::pressed()` function. Though there might also be some deeper entity deciding popup directions, I don't know.
